  "query_preview": "(Today through Tuesday)...\nIssued at 252 AM EDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nEarly This Morning...\n\nEnergy riding around an upper high with help from a surface front \nhas been generating convection from northern Missouri into the \nnorthern forecast area. Looking upstream, there may be a brief lull \nas convection remains just west and north of the area, but more will \nmove in closer to sunrise. Outflow from the convection has reached \nthe I-70 corridor, and this may spark an isolated shower in that \narea. Will continue with mainly chance PoPs from about I-70 north \nthrough 12Z.\n\nSome gusty winds and heavy rain are possible, but odds of severe \nremain low given lessening instability.\n\nToday...\n\nSome stronger upper energy looks to bring showers and some storms to \nportions of the northern forecast area after 12Z, so will go with \nhigh chance to likely category PoPs there. Will keep chance PoPs \nsouth of this area this morning in case outflow is enough to trigger \nmore isolated to scattered convection.\n\nThere looks to be less upper support this afternoon for convection, \nbut with various old outflows in the area as well as the surface \nfront, will go with at least slight chance PoPs most areas this \nafternoon. The far southern area may be far enough from outflow and \nclose enough to the upper high to remain dry. Severe parameters look \nlow enough that severe storms are not expected, but a gusty storm is \npossible. Locally heavy rain will remain a threat with a moist \natmosphere.\n\nConvection/clouds will help keep temperatures cooler across the \nnorthern forecast area, so went middle to upper 80s. The central \nforecast area looks more uncertain thanks to the questions about how \nmuch convection will be generated by outflows and the surface front. \nWill go lower 90s there. The south should still be able to reach the \nmiddle 90s. Heat indices will reach around 100 again this afternoon \nfor much of the area.\n\nTonight and Thursday...\n\nMore energy riding around the slowly retreating upper high along \nwith the old surface front will keep chances for convection around, \nmainly across the northern half of the area. Similar to today, \nclouds/convection Thursday will keep temperatures cooler north with \nhot conditions persisting south. Heat indices will remain around 100 \nsouth during Thursday afternoon. \n\nFriday and beyond...\n\nThe upper high will continue to gradually retreat southwest. The \nsurface front will sink far enough south initially to keep PoPs low \non Friday, but it will return north again on Saturday as an upper \nwave interacts with the front. This will bring more rain chances, \nmainly north. \n\nAfter a brief reprieve from heat for many areas Friday, hot \nconditions return on Saturday as the front moves back north.\n\nSunday into next week, larger upper waves moving through will keep \nchances for rain around. Cooler air will filter back into the area, \nwith highs by Tuesday in the upper 70s to middle 80s.",
